  "name": "gorogoro plus",
  "description": "Gorogoro plus, shogi on a board five files wide and six ranks deep, as PyChess plays it (Gorogoro+). Each side has a king, two golds, two silvers and three pawns, the pawns already meeting the enemy's in the middle, and starts with a lance and a knight in hand. Captured pieces change sides and may be dropped back. Pawns, silvers, lances and knights promote in the last two ranks, on a move into, inside or out of them: the pawn, lance and knight to a gold, the silver to a gold too; a piece that could never move again must promote, and may not be dropped where it could never move. A pawn may not be dropped on a file already holding one of its side's pawns, nor to give mate. One departure, an edge rule: a fourth repetition is a draw, where the shogi rule this game follows makes perpetual check a loss for the checking side.",
